.TH SAMBA-AD-BACKEND 1 "October 2026" "samba-powershell 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
samba-ad-backend \- backend process of the SambaAD PowerShell module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B samba-ad-backend
.RB [ \-h ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.BR request | status
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B samba-ad-backend
is the Python half of the SambaAD PowerShell module shipped by
samba-powershell. The cmdlets, such as
.BR Get-ADUser ,
start it once per call, write one JSON request on its standard input and read
one JSON response from its standard output. It reads the directory through the
samba-adws Active Directory Web Services client, authenticated with the
caller's Kerberos ticket.
.PP
It is an internal process boundary, not a command meant for interactive use:
use the cmdlets from
.BR pwsh (1)
instead.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B request
Reads one request from standard input and writes one response to standard
output. It exits 0 when the response reports success and 1 when it reports a
failure.
.TP
.B status
Reports whether the backend can start, without touching the network. It prints
.I samba-ad-backend: ready
and exits 0.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Shows a summary of the commands.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Prints the version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KRB5CCNAME
The Kerberos credential cache the backend authenticates with, inherited from
the cmdlet's process.
.TP
.B SAMBA_AD_SERVER
The domain controller used when a request names none.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pwsh (1),
.BR kinit (1)
